        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/embedding/CachedEmbeddingCreator.java#L209-L223",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:41030ecdf34c497066b23d0dc7a7f600f6cdb1d3b83e3bb2289ce7e334dd38cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_17bd99d5f5414552bc89b52a303cad3f",
      "statement": "In tryToFixWithLength, failure attribution uses jtokkit: if the configured model name has no known encoding, or the full content counts fewer than MAX_TOKEN_LENGTH tokens, the original failure was not a token-length problem and the method throws IllegalArgumentException instead of returning an embedding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/embedding/CachedEmbeddingCreator.java#L224-L229",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c825d3318e4087c03c000a1b92e672566098542d8c0a9bac909bb73b8905dc3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_16b3e7b1f2484d1fb1a1060915092aaa",
      "statement": "MAX_TOKEN_LENGTH is 8000, deliberately below the 8192 limit the source comment notes for ada; the binary search over character offsets converges on the shortest prefix that reaches 8000 tokens (the boundary prefix just past the conservative threshold), embeds that prefix, and stores the vector only under the _fixed_ key via putViaInternalKey — the original content key never receives a vector, so untruncated text can never be answered with the truncated embedding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/embedding/CachedEmbeddingCreator.java#L231-L250",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:695343e3833b1b56826dae8f9dea518504cfc3850feb8ae697b7e95168c08b0a:"
        },
        {
